{{if .Has "go"}}
## Go Mutation Rules

These rules govern Go code under {{.PathsOf "go"}}. Go is NOT a functional language — idiomatic Go uses pointer receivers and in-place mutation. Follow these concrete rules:

### ALLOWED (idiomatic Go, do NOT avoid)
```go
// ✅ Pointer receiver modifying own fields
func (s *Service) SetWorker(w *Worker) { s.worker = w }

// ✅ Scan into struct fields
rows.Scan(&p.UserID, &p.Nickname, &p.Level)

// ✅ Building a struct then passing pointer to repository
player := &Player{UserID: id, Status: "active"}
repo.Create(ctx, player)

// ✅ Accumulating results in a slice
var items []*Item
for rows.Next() { items = append(items, &it) }
```

### FORBIDDEN (causes bugs)
```go
// ❌ Mutating a struct received by value (caller won't see changes)
func process(p Player) { p.Level = 10 }  // BUG: caller's copy unchanged

// ❌ Mutating shared/cached data without copy
cached := cache.Get(key)
cached.Level = 99        // BUG: corrupts cache for other readers
// FIX: copy := *cached; copy.Level = 99; use &copy

// ❌ Mutating a slice/map parameter that caller doesn't expect to change
func enrich(items []*Item) { items[0].Quantity = 0 }  // BUG: caller's data changed
// FIX: return new slice, or document mutation in function name (e.g., MutateItems)

// ❌ Storing a reference to request data that may be reused
func (s *Service) Handle(req *Request) {
    s.lastReq = req  // BUG: req may be pooled/reused by framework
}
```

### ONE RULE
**Own data → mutate freely. Shared/received data → copy first or document mutation in the function name.**
{{else}}
## Mutation

**Own data → mutate freely. Shared/received data → copy first or document mutation in the function name.** Data taken from a cache, passed in by a caller, or held by more than one owner is not yours to change in place.
{{end}}
## File Organization

MANY SMALL FILES > FEW LARGE FILES:
- High cohesion, low coupling
- At most 800 lines per file; generated code is not counted
- Extract utilities (e.g., converters, helpers) from large files when possible
- Organize by feature/domain, not by type

A type's methods may be split across several files by concern (core use cases, background work, validation) to keep every file under the limit. The type itself stays one.

## Errors and Input Validation

Handle or return every error; never swallow one. What a caller may see and what goes only to the server log is in `security.md` (錯誤訊息洩漏); which layer validates what is in `security.md` (輸入驗證) and in the repo's architecture document.

## Code Quality Checklist

Before marking work complete:
- [ ] Functions are small (<50 lines)
- [ ] Files are focused (at most 800 lines; see File Organization)
- [ ] No deep nesting (>4 levels)
- [ ] Proper error handling
- [ ] No hardcoded values (server: constants or configuration{{if .Has "dotnet"}}; client: visual parameters in theme resources, design numbers in data files, neither written into C#{{end}})
- [ ] No mutation of shared/cached/received data without copy
